-- **set-ridge.** Two unframed vignettes on one continuous warm-paper ground. Left: a high dry ridge of chalk-white rock and bleached pale grass under hard flat midday light with short shadows, a narrow pale road running along the spine, a few twisted dead gray pines, wide hazy azurite valleys falling away on both sides; above the road, a tall tooth of white rock — the crag — with a dark cave-mouth at its top. Right: the same ridge road further along in long amber late-afternoon light, long shadows across the white rock, the crag small behind. Bone, ash, chalk and hazy blue; no green fields, no water, no buildings, no fruit, no figures, no gold. Never the ochre dust road of the earlier volume or a sand-coloured river plain.
